---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_URL, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy policy of Trip Expense Ledger: trips stay in your browser" description="What the per diem and mileage calculators process: no cookie, no account, no destination or travel date stored or sent. Your rights under the GDPR and the US state privacy laws." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This policy covers {SITE_URL}. A travel plan says where you will be and when; this site was built so that it never needs to know. The publisher is established in France, so the EU General Data Protection Regulation applies to every visitor, and residents of US states with a consumer privacy law keep at least the rights listed here.</p>
    <p>No cookie is set by this site, and nothing you type is stored on your device or sent to a server.</p>
    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>2. What stays in your browser</h2>
    <p>Destinations, dates, miles, meals, vehicle and price figures are processed by the page on your own device. Nothing is sent to us or to anyone else. The city list and the ZIP table are downloaded from this site the first time you search, the same files for everybody. Once you change a field, your inputs are written into the page address so that the share link works; whoever receives that link can read them.</p>
    <h2>3. What is processed</h2>
    <h3>Hosting logs</h3><p>GitHub, the host, records the IP address, time, page and browser of each request to keep the service secure. Legal basis: legitimate interest. Retention follows GitHub's policy.</p>
    {CLARITY_ID
      ? <><h3>Stability monitoring, without cookies</h3><p>To find broken pages, the site loads Microsoft Clarity (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited) in its cookie-free mode: errors, loading times and clicks that lead nowhere, per page view, with page content and inputs masked. Microsoft receives the technical data of the request, including the IP address. Legal basis: legitimate interest (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). Block clarity.ms or write to us to object.</p></>
      : <><h3>No analytics</h3><p>No audience measurement, advertising or social media script is loaded. Should a stability monitoring tool be added, this page will name it first.</p></>}
    <h3>E-mails</h3><p>If you write, your address and message are kept to answer and deleted three years after the last exchange.</p>
    <h2>4. No sale, no sharing</h2><p>We sell and share no personal information and build no profiles.</p>
    <h2>5. Transfers</h2><p>GitHub, Inc. is in the United States; request data may be processed there under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>Access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability and objection: write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, answer within one month. Complaints: {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>).</p>
    <h2>7. Children</h2><p>The site is meant for adults planning business travel and collects nothing from children under 13.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a> and the <a href={route('terms', lang)}>legal notice</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
